From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:36:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/32] feat(dashboard): serve the desktop web build at /app
 behind the auth gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HERMES_WEB_APP_DIST (mirroring HERMES_WEB_DIST) opts a dashboard process
into serving apps/desktop/dist-web at /app: hashed assets under /app/assets
with the immutable cache header, real dist files served as files, and the
index (no-store) carrying the same token/auth bootstrap the dashboard SPA
gets — token injected exactly once on loopback, never when gated. The mount
registers inside mount_spa() BEFORE the catch-all route (a later /app would
be unreachable — Starlette matches in registration order), redirects /app to
the canonical /app/ so the build's relative asset URLs resolve correctly,
and stays off entirely in headless serve mode and when the env is unset
(byte-identical catch-all baseline, covered by test). The gate is
default-deny, so /app sits behind the cookie session with no extra wiring.
